pletely different, rarer, and far more dangerous beast. --- **So, to sum up:** The news story you remember doesn’t prove a chain reaction; it demonstrates an extreme **system-wide pressure failure**. The fires broke out in multiple places not because a flame traveled along the pipe, but because the same excessive pressure arrived at every home at once, creating explosive mixtures inside them. The initial explanation—that gas pipes themselves don’t act as fuses—still stands, but the culprit that day wasn’t a flame front; it was the invisible, instantaneous spread of a pressure wave. It’s a scary and important nuance, and you’re sharp for connecting the two.
